imx585-dkms (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * imx585: recheck dependent limits when applying batched controls
  * Document IMX585 writes outside the standard register map
  * imx585: keep timing writes tied to the programmed sensor mode
  * imx585: advertise eight initialization frames after standby
  * imx585: start master timing after standby stabilization
  * imx585: enforce the combined Clear HDR gain limits
  * imx585: report the Bayer order selected by sensor flips
  * imx585: reject reversed Clear HDR selection thresholds
  * imx585: route private timing writes through the V4L2 controls
  * imx585: preserve integration when the frame length changes
  * imx585: advertise the sensor's two-line timing resolution
  * imx585: derive blanking limits from the active sensor instance
  * imx585: preserve fixed sync selector bits and pin direction
  * imx585: restore the RAW10 frame length at 2079 Mbit/s
  * imx585: use ten-bit conversion for 1080p binning
  * imx585: preserve ADC-specific timing at RAW10 stream start

 -- Dale Ghent <daleg@elemental.org>  Thu, 26 Nov 2026 20:56:47 -0700

imx585-dkms (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of IMX585 DKMS driver package
  * Support for Sony IMX585 CMOS image sensor
  * DKMS integration for automatic kernel module rebuilding
  * Device tree overlay compilation and installation
  * Support for various sensor configurations:
    - 2-lane and 4-lane MIPI CSI-2 modes
    - Monochrome variants
    - Configurable link frequencies
    - Sync modes (internal-leader, internal-follower, external)
    - RAW10 and RAW12 pixel formats

 -- Dale Ghent <daleg@elemental.org>  Mon, 02 Jun 2026 21:23:00 +0000
